  "verbalization": "Curcumene is associated with HL-60 through a series of molecular interactions, primarily via Lysine-specific demethylase 2A (LSD2A). This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including [(2S,9R,13R,14S,15R,17R)-14-acetyloxy-16-hydroxy-4-methoxy-2,6,14,17-tetramethyl-3,11-dioxo-10-oxatetracyclo[7.7.1.02,7.013,17]heptadec-4-en-15-yl] acetate, Kaempferol 3-Neohesperidoside, and Megastigma-4,6(Z),8(Z)-triene. These compounds are all linked to HL-60, a human promyelocytic leukemia cell line, suggesting that Curcumene may exert its effects through a common pathway involving LSD2A. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Curcumene's interaction with HL-60 is mediated through LSD2A, which is a key target of multiple bioactive compounds. The varying scores across the paths suggest that the strength of the relationship may depend on the specific compound involved, but the consistent association between Curcumene and HL-60 through LSD2A provides a robust mechanism for the observed effects."
